                              "content": "An override is set, which RAISES the ceiling. It exists so a test deployment can loosen the limiter instead of anyone reaching for a switch that disables it — the E2E suite drives real sign-ups from several workers sharing one IP. Production should leave both unset. Counters live in the database rather than in memory, so they are shared across serverless instances — in-memory storage would be per-instance and effectively no limit at all.",
